# QA

Follow `docs/sdlc.md`. Do not QA a pull request you authored or reviewed. Report results on the pull request.

From the repo root:

```bash
(cd rust && cargo test --workspace)
cargo run --manifest-path rust/Cargo.toml -p timberbot-drills -- offline --cases scenarios/eval-cases.json
cargo run --manifest-path rust/Cargo.toml -p timberbot-drills -- drills
python3 scripts/lint_skills.py
```

Staged drills pass only with 0 deaths and 0 contamination. Confirm GitHub Actions is green on the pull request. A merge also needs reviewer approval. When the diff touches `timberbot/`, the pull request must name the `timberbot-mod-<version>.zip` rebuild (`scripts/package-mod.ps1` or `scripts/package-mod.sh`) before QA signs off.
